On $CC^n$ the inner product is
$ (bold(z), bold(w)) = sum_(i=1)^n overline(z_i) w_i. $
It is Hermitian, $(bold(z), bold(w)) = overline((bold(w), bold(z)))$; linear in the second argument and anti-linear in the first, $(mu bold(z), bold(w)) = overline(mu) (bold(z), bold(w))$; and positive definite, $(bold(z), bold(z)) = sum_j abs(z_j)^2 >= 0$ with equality iff $bold(z) = bold(0)$. These axioms define an inner product on any vector space over $RR$ or $CC$.
